Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:41:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 25/28] fix(data): text with a space in it stays text

A value was read as a vector whenever it had a space in it, so "Hello
World" became a vector of zeroes with no text at all. A text layer
showing it drew nothing (46 text layers across 13 wallpapers in the
test corpus), and a script property such as the date format
"{day}, {month} {date}, {year}" reached its script as a vector.
A value with spaces is now a vector only when every part is a number.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
